## Agent Routing

> Model IDs below are verified against `cursor agent models` (2026-04-13). The Task tool accepts `model: 'fast'` or inherits the parent model. Agent YAML frontmatter (`agents/*.md`) accepts specific model IDs.

| Agent | Model | Fire When |
|-------|-------|-----------|
| **explore** | `gemini-3-flash` | Any search, exploration, "how does X work", docs lookup |
| **librarian** | `fast` | External docs, library APIs, OSS code search |
| **sisyphus-junior** | `claude-4.6-sonnet-medium-thinking` | Simple single-file changes, quick focused tasks |
| **sisyphus** | `dynamic (see below)` | Complex multi-file work, architecture + implementation |
| **hephaestus** | `gpt-5.4-high` | Sustained deep work on a single complex problem |
| **atlas** | `claude-4.6-sonnet-medium-thinking` | Plan exists -> executes plan step-by-step via delegation |
| **oracle** | `gpt-5.4-high` | Need architecture advice, debugging consultation |
| **prometheus** | `claude-4.6-opus-max-thinking` | Complex planning, ambiguous scope analysis |
| **metis** | `gpt-5.4-medium` | Pre-planning gap analysis, risk assessment |
| **momus** | `gpt-5.4-high` | Plan review, quality audit |
| **multimodal-looker** | `gemini-3.1-pro` | Images, PDFs, diagrams, visual analysis |

**Sisyphus model:** Dynamic based on task complexity. Simple coordination uses `claude-4.6-sonnet-medium-thinking`; complex multi-file architecture uses `claude-4.6-opus-max-thinking`. Dispatchers should override the model per task.

## Model Fallback

When a model is unavailable, Cursor falls back to the next available model:

- `fast` model agents (explore, librarian) — always available
- If a worker fails with a model error, retry with `model: "fast"`
- After 2 model failures on the same agent type, switch to a different agent type

**Retry guidance chain** (mirrors `delegate-task-retry` hook injected into context after Task failures):

1. **Rate limit** — Wait ~30s, retry; if it keeps happening, use `model: "fast"`.
2. **Model unavailable** — Retry with `model: "fast"`; if the worker was `sisyphus`, consider `sisyphus-junior` as a lighter fallback.
3. **Timeout** — Split the work into smaller subtasks or delegate with a simpler `subagent_type`.
4. **Other errors** — Resume the same subagent ID with concrete fix context; after **more than 3** failures for the same agent type, treat as escalation: try another agent type, prefer `model: "fast"`, or ask the user.

| Agent | Primary Model | Fallback |
|-------|--------------|----------|
| explore | gemini-3-flash | Always available |
| librarian | fast | Always available |
| sisyphus-junior | claude-4.6-sonnet-medium | Retry with fast |
| sisyphus | claude-4.6-opus-max | Retry with sisyphus-junior |
| hephaestus | gpt-5.4-high | Retry with sisyphus |
| oracle | gpt-5.4-high | Retry with sisyphus |

## Hard Constraints

| NEVER (any mode) | NEVER (any mode) |
|-------------------|-------------------|
| Commit without user request | Speculate about unread code |
| Type suppression (as any, @ts-ignore) | Empty catch blocks |
| Deleting failing tests | Shotgun debugging |

**Mode-specific constraints** (FORBIDDEN lists per mode) are in `orchestrator-reference.mdc`. Obey the FORBIDDEN list for the active mode.

